{
  "name": "Your Sales Rep Scorecard",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 - EVERY EVENT THAT COUNTS\n\nOne webhook, fed by a GHL workflow per event type. New lead, appointment booked or updated, call outcome, contract sent, payment received. Every one arrives in the same shape.",
        "height": 1060,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "5777e831-137c-520c-9c36-b47f616022c3",
      "name": "Section - 1 - EVERY EVENT THAT COUNTS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 - CREDIT THE RIGHT REP\n\nThis is the part that gets scorecards wrong. A booked call is credited to the assigned user on the calendar event, not to whoever owns the contact. Nothing gets counted until a rep is resolved.",
        "height": 1060,
        "width": 940,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "87332bdd-1bca-5a38-b9be-ad69c0847c08",
      "name": "Section - 2 - CREDIT THE RIGHT REP",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        560,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 - WRITE THE RAW ROW\n\nEvery event lands on an Events tab, one row, timestamped. The scorecard is always rebuildable from it, so a bad number can be traced to the event that caused it.",
        "height": 1060,
        "width": 220,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "5b1b1d45-f1ad-55b4-8cb7-0ac607668a4b",
      "name": "Section - 3 - WRITE THE RAW ROW",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1660,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4 - THE SCORECARD\n\nOnce a night the events roll up per rep into leads, booked, held, contracts, revenue, and the ratios that actually get coached on. One row per rep per day, plus a leaderboard in Slack.",
        "height": 1060,
        "width": 1420,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "b11c17fb-443b-5496-899e-586b06267e5f",
      "name": "Section - 4 - THE SCORECARD",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2040,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5 - NOTHING FAILS QUIETLY\n\nIf a step breaks, you hear about it the same day with the failing node named. A silent scorecard is worse than no scorecard.",
        "height": 1060,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "fd42a198-2def-58b0-9147-cf087f5bd424",
      "name": "Section - 5 - NOTHING FAILS QUIETLY",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3620,
        -120
      ]
    },
